  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "One goal for both teams",
  "description": "Seven players, one ball and one goal in an area of about 25 × 25 metres. One player goes in goal and the other six play three v three. The goalkeeper stands with their back to the pitch and throws the ball out backwards, so nobody knows where it will land.\n\nThe team that gets the ball attacks and tries to score, and the other team defends until they win it – then they attack instead, at the same goal and the same goalkeeper. After a goal or a save, the goalkeeper throws it out again. Change goalkeeper after every goal or two, or every three minutes, so everyone gets a turn.\n\nVariant: only the team that wins the ball after the throw may score. If the other team wins it, they pass it to the goalkeeper, who throws it out again. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Get to the ball quickly when it is thrown – and switch quickly when it changes hands."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Feint, dribble and pass: there are many ways to reach the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defenders: stand between the ball and the goal."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: move with the ball and be ready – the shot can come from anywhere."
    }
  ],
